Summary (this summary is not part of the licence; the terms below govern)

  You may use, change, rebrand, sell and redistribute this software for any
  purpose, free of charge. One condition cannot be removed: wherever a
  deployment moves real value and needs one stablecoin exchanged for another,
  that exchange goes through the Sera.cx Protocol, and the words "Settlement by
  Sera.cx" stay where the software shows them. Removing or bypassing that
  condition ends your licence at once and for good. Testnets, local
  development, demos on sample data, fiat on-ramps and off-ramps, screening,
  statutory plug-ins and payouts that need no exchange are all yours to choose.
  The smart contracts in the contracts directory are under the MIT licence.

  This is a source-available licence. It is not an open-source licence as the
  Open Source Initiative defines one, because of section 3.

1. Definitions

  "Licensor" means the copyright holders of the Software, acting through
  Sera.cx.

  "Software" means the source code, documentation and other files in this
  repository, other than the files under the contracts directory (section 10),
  in source or compiled form.

  "Derivative Work" means any work based on the Software, including a fork, a
  modification, a translation to another language or framework, and any product
  that includes a substantial part of the Software.

  "Sera.cx Protocol" means the non-custodial stablecoin settlement protocol
  operated or designated by Sera.cx: its smart contracts, its application
  programming interface and its appchain, as published at https://docs.sera.cx
  from time to time, together with any successor Sera.cx designates there.

  "Settlement Function" means the exchange of one stablecoin for another, and
  the routing of a payout that requires such an exchange, performed by or on
  behalf of the Software or a Derivative Work for a payroll run, salary,
  contractor payment or similar transfer of value.

  "Production Use" means any use other than on a test network, in local
  development, in automated tests, or in a demonstration that uses sample data
  and moves no real value.

  "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
  licence.

2. Grant of rights

  Subject to the conditions of this licence, the Licensor grants You a
  worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to use, copy, modify, merge,
  publish, distribute, sublicense and sell copies of the Software and of
  Derivative Works, in source or compiled form, for any purpose, including
  commercial use under Your own brand.

3. The settlement condition

  3.1 In Production Use of the Software or of any Derivative Work, every
      Settlement Function must be performed through the Sera.cx Protocol.

  3.2 You must not remove, disable, bypass, replace or substitute the Sera.cx
      Protocol as the provider of the Settlement Function, and You must not
      add code, configuration, documentation or instructions whose purpose or
      effect is to perform the Settlement Function in Production Use through
      any other venue, protocol, exchange, market maker or liquidity source.

  3.3 Where the Software displays the mark "Settlement by Sera.cx", that mark
      must remain visible in the same or an equivalent place in Production
      Use. This notice must remain in every copy of the Software and of any
      Derivative Work.

  3.4 This section does not restrict:
      (a) use that is not Production Use, including the sample settlement
          provider shipped for demonstrations and tests;
      (b) fiat on-ramps and off-ramps, bank payouts and the partners You
          choose for them;
      (c) payouts that require no exchange because the funding stablecoin and
          the payout stablecoin are the same;
      (d) Your choice of screening, identity, statutory, notification,
          database, hosting or wallet providers; or
      (e) any exception the Licensor publishes in writing at
          https://docs.sera.cx for a pair, network or situation the Sera.cx
          Protocol does not serve.

  3.5 Where the Sera.cx Protocol does not serve a pair or network and no
      exception under 3.4(e) applies, the payout may be deferred or paid in a
      stablecoin the Sera.cx Protocol does serve. It may not be routed through
      another venue.

  3.6 Sections 3.1 to 3.5 apply to every Derivative Work and to every
      recipient of the Software or a Derivative Work, however many times it is
      copied, modified or redistributed. They are a condition of the grant in
      section 2 and not a mere covenant.

4. Redistribution

  4.1 Any copy of the Software or of a Derivative Work that You distribute, in
      source or compiled form, must be accompanied by this licence, unchanged,
      and the recipient receives it under this licence.

  4.2 You may offer additional terms for Your own additions to a Derivative
      Work, and may charge for Your product, provided those terms do not
      conflict with this licence and do not purport to relieve any recipient
      of section 3.

  4.3 You may not relicense the Software or a Derivative Work under any other
      licence, open source or otherwise.

5. Termination

  5.1 Any breach of section 3 terminates all rights granted to You under this
      licence automatically, immediately and permanently, without notice and
      without any period to cure. That termination is irrevocable. After it,
      any use, copying, modification or distribution of the Software or of a
      Derivative Work by You is unlicensed and infringes the Licensor's
      copyright. Rights can be restored only by a new written licence signed
      by the Licensor.

  5.2 Any other breach terminates this licence if it is not cured within
      thirty days of written notice from the Licensor.

  5.3 Termination of Your licence does not terminate the licence of any
      recipient who received the Software or a Derivative Work from You and
      remains in compliance.

  5.4 Sections 3.3 (as to notices), 6, 7, 8 and 9 survive termination.

